From 6df53e7cddf25bd6106875062b4fc1250485518d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Colin Catlin <colin.catlin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:52:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] review: timing fixes (UNVERIFIED on air - do not merge
 without A/B)

UNVERIFIED: these changes touch radio/scheduler timing and have NOT been
proven by a concurrent two-receiver on-air A/B. The room was at ~32% loss
on both receivers (only trainer #52233 on air), which voids any loss
comparison. ztest-verified only. Do not merge into review/2026-10-31 or
master until an A/B (see memory: promicro-clone-bringup, ant-bench-loss-floor)
shows no regression.

- A14-1 radiant_radio_nrf.c: detect a START compare that is already in the
  past (clear event before CC write, ETIME path, radiant_dbg_start_late)
- A13-1 radiant_radio_nrf.c: CLOCK_LOCK/UNLOCK (ZLI lock when the core
  callback is deferred), radiant_dbg_clock_back
- A14-2 radiant_radio_nrf.c: CORE_CB_BODY_MAX bound + BUILD_ASSERT; the
  oversize branch sets body_len 0
- A9-3 radiant_sched.c/.h: reclaim an armed operation that never terminated
  (RADIANT_SCHED_ARMED_STALE_US, armed_stale stat)
- A8-4 radiant_sched.c: RX expiry accounts for phy_lead()
- C5-1 radiant_radio_nrf_gate_mpsl.c: BLOCKED/CANCELLED back off the class
  that was actually placed, not the current one

Tests (each fails under its named mutation, passes fixed):
  test_sched: test_an_operation_that_never_terminates_is_reclaimed (A9-3)
  test_lr: test_a_window_inside_the_phy_switch_is_missed_not_skipped (A8-4)
  test_gate: test_an_inline_block_backs_off_the_class_that_was_refused (C5-1)
ztest on nRF5340 DK: main 839/839, gate 32/32, api 52/52.
